        "id": 54438,
        "name": "Koey",
        "username": "Koey",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koey/{size}/2187_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-21T06:57:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Regarding the Legacy/Baron Blade - I always find they both can take a lot of damage. Where as Blade throws minions and platforms to distract you from hitting him. And the whole terralunar lazer you need to deal with. While legacy tanks the damage with his body. And it seems they both let others do their work for them most of the time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Visionary and Dreamer I can see as Visionary has managed to control has mast and superior power while her younger self lacks control and instead has sporadic power surge of projections. Also to be fair isn't Dreamers deck all about controlling the damage on how to protect the dreamer, sort of contrasting the Cocoon where Visionary can tank all damage while Dreamer requires Heroes to tank it for her.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Side note: what does everyone feel about the new Lose conditions you can get from Silve Gulch? Still unsure of the reasoning behind the portal card that lets you discard to discard the top environment.</p>",
        "post_number": 73,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:28:53.323Z",
